From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 18:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add UpCloud capacity provider

Implements the substrate-specific providerkit.Backend (+ Deleter) for UpCloud
cloud servers under providers/upcloud/, certified via the credential-free
fake backend.

- Lifecycle: Create clones an OS template + pins an SSH host key; Configure and
  Drain EnsureRunning first (a tracked server can be stopped out-of-band) then
  deliver the bootstrap blob / drain over SSH with the host key verified against
  the pinned fingerprint; Delete stops then DeleteServerAndStorages (storage is
  a separate billable resource), idempotent if already gone.
- On-demand only: capacity_type=ON_DEMAND, interruption_probability=0; resources
  (operator-declared per-replica) kept distinct from allocatable (Plans-API
  hardware total).
- Auto backend selection: fake unless UPCLOUD_USERNAME/PASSWORD and --zone are
  set; the fake models stop-out-of-band so the EnsureRunning path has real tests.
- Operator-first docs (docs/) and deploy artifacts (distroless image, Helm chart
  one release per zone, API sub-account + SSH Secret wiring).

make certify-upcloud passes (upstream baseline + extension suite); make
report-upcloud PROFILE=core,cloud -> VERDICT CERTIFIED.

